  "mechanisms": [
    "Misophonic subjects assign aberrantly higher salience to trigger sounds due to specific hyperactivity in the anterior insular cortex (AIC).",
    "Abnormal functional connectivity between AIC and regions of the default mode network (DMN) (vmPFC, PMC, hippocampus, amygdala) prevents misophonic subjects from disengaging AIC from memories and contextual associations related to trigger sounds.",
    "Altered myelination in vmPFC provides a structural basis for the observed abnormal functional connectivity.",
    "AIC activity mediates heightened autonomic responses (HR, GSR) to trigger sounds in misophonic individuals.",
    "Misophonia involves abnormal interoceptive processing, as evidenced by higher interoceptive sensibility scores and AIC dysfunction."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "Group (misophonic vs. control)",
    "Sound type (trigger vs. unpleasant vs. neutral)"
  ],
